#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "On the search page, open the <b>Comments</b> tab to search what people wrote in comments (a guild's own search has it too). Words, \"phrases\" and <code>-words</code> are looked for in the comment's text. These operators work on comments: <code>%(from_op)s</code>, <code>%(in_op)s</code> (where the comment is: its post's guild, topic or curation), <code>%(since)s</code>, <code>%(until)s</code>, <code>%(after)s</code>, <code>%(before)s</code>, <code>%(on)s</code>, <code>%(min_votes)s</code>, <code>%(is_ai)s</code> and <code>%(is_partnership)s</code>. The ones about a post's own content (<code>%(has)s</code>, <code>%(lang)s</code>, <code>%(domain)s</code>, <code>%(url)s</code>, <code>%(flair)s</code>, <code>%(is_forward)s</code>, <code>%(min_comments)s</code>) are left out with a note."
msgstr "Na página de pesquisa, abra o <b>Observações</b> tab para pesquisar o que as pessoas escreveram em comentários (a própria pesquisa de uma guild também tem). Palavras, frases e <code>-words</code> são procurados no texto do comentário. Estes operadores trabalham em comentários: <code>%(from_op)s</code>, <code>%(in_op)s</code> (onde o comentário é: guild do seu post, tópico ou alimentação curado), <code>%(since)s</code>, <code>%(until)s</code>, <code>%(after)s</code>, <code>%(before)s</code>, <code>%(on)s</code>, <code>%(min_votes)s</code>, <code>%(is_ai)s</code> e <code>%(is_partnership)s</code>. Aqueles sobre o próprio conteúdo de um post (<code>%(has)s</code>, <code>%(lang)s</code>, <code>%(domain)s</code>, <code>%(url)s</code>, <code>%(flair)s</code>, <code>%(is_forward)s</code>, <code>%(min_comments)s</code>) são deixados de fora com uma nota."

